program Family logic.
note Models translate the story into facts; the kernel's Datalog engine does the multi-hop reasoning, which small models get wrong when they try it in their heads.

given story: Text = """Ada is the mother of Ben. Ben is the father of Cleo and of Dov.
Cleo is the mother of Eli. Dov is the father of Fay. Fay is the mother of Gus."""

define Link as Record {parent: Text, child: Text}.
ask links: List of Link "List every parent-child relation the story states, using first names exactly as written." from story with effort=high
ensure len(links) = 6 else retry because "the story states six parent-child relations".

for l in links do
  fact parent(lower(l.parent), lower(l.child)).
end.

rule ancestor(X, Y) if parent(X, Y).
rule ancestor(X, Z) if parent(X, Y) and ancestor(Y, Z).
rule cousin(X, Y) if parent(P, X) and parent(Q, Y) and parent(G, P) and parent(G, Q) and P != Q.

let descendants = query ancestor(ada, Who).
let cousins_of_eli = query cousin(eli, C).
assert "gus" in descendants.
show descendants as "everyone descended from Ada".
show cousins_of_eli as "Eli's first cousins".
